WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.136
-President Trump has settled

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.437
on his closing argument
for the midterms --

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.405
lying about healthcare,
immigration,

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:07.640
and a made-up tax cut.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.776
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:13.980
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.549
-After a series
of explosive devices

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:19.351
was sent to prominent Democrats
and CNN yesterday,

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:21.153
President Trump
flew to Wisconsin

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:24.590
to campaign for GOP
Senate candidate Leah Vukmir.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.793
You could tell Trump
was trying to restrain himself.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.228
In fact, throughout the rally,

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:31.498
he kept bragging to the crowd
about how nice he was being.

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:34.634
-The Democrats
are for higher taxes,

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:38.938
more regulation, and more
top-down government control.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.041
[ Audience booing ]

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:45.812
And by the way, do you see
how nice I'm behaving tonight?

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:49.048
This is, like --
Have you ever seen this?

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.951
We're all behaving very well.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.554
And, hopefully,
we can keep it that way, right?

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.688
[ Cheering ]

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.690
We're gonna keep it that way.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.360
Leah's radical, far-left
opponent is Tammy Baldwin...

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.932
[ Audience booing ]

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:09.535
...who wants a socialist
takeover of healthcare.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:13.139
[ Audience booing ]

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.241
You know, I'm trying
to say that very nicely.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.076
I'm trying to --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:18.378
See, normally I'd scream,

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.880
"They want
a socialist takeover."

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.016
Now I say,
"Wants a socialist takeover."

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.149
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:25.951
I'm trying to be nice.

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:29.222
-Man, low-energy Trump
is so weird.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.990
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.458
It's like --

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.760
[ Applause ]

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.996
It's like seeing
that neighborhood dog

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.965
who's always digging
through everyone's trash

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.534
suddenly moping around
with a cone on his head.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.669
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.171
Hey, maybe don't make it clear

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.307
that being nice
wasn't your first choice.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.276
You're like a cannibal
who wants credit

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.178
for just licking people's faces.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.412
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.381
"Isn't it great
that I haven't taken a bite?"

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.649
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.183
You're an adult.
you don't get credit

00:01:58.183 --> 00:02:00.152
for doing something
adults are supposed to do.

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:03.222
Someone sent bombs to several
major political figures,

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:05.524
and Trump's acting like a kid
whose parents forced him

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:08.427
to wear a suit
for the family Christmas photo.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:09.829
I'm surprised he didn't
end the rally

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.497
by turning to Mike Pence
and saying,

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:14.167
"I was nice!
Can I have my ice cream now?!"

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:16.869
Also, listen to Trump --

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:21.040
[ Applause ]

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.975
Listen to Trump's
impression of himself.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:26.245
It's almost like
he knows how crazy he is.

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:27.380
-See, normally I'd scream,

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.882
"They want
a socialist takeover!"

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.685
Now I say,
"Wants a socialist takeover."

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.254
-I've said it before,
and I'll say it again --

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.823
Donald Trump has the best
Donald Trump impression.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:40.459
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:42.194
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:43.829
"Have you guys --
Have you guys ever noticed

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:46.165
that thing
where I'm all, like, crazy?"

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.869
This rally was just
the latest in a series

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.171
Trump has been doing
to campaign for Republicans

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.639
in the closing days
before the midterms.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:56.542
Now, if there's one refrain
you hear more than any other

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.578
at these rallies,
it's his false claim

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.747
that he's accomplished more
than any president in history.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:02.782
But tellingly,
Republicans are not actually

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:05.051
talking about any of those
supposed accomplishments.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.320
Just take their signature
piece of legislation,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.322
the massive tax cut they gave
to corporations and the wealthy.

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:13.893
That tax cut is so unpopular
that rather than campaign on it,

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.862
Trump is just making up
a completely new tax cut

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:18.831
specifically for
the middle class

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.834
that he claims Republicans
are about to pass.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.336
-We are looking at putting in

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:26.606
a very major tax cut
for middle-income people.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.941
And if we do that,
it'll be sometime just prior,

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:30.576
I would say, to November.

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.912
We are going to be putting in,

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.214
and are studying
very deeply right now,

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:39.985
round the clock, a major tax cut
for middle-income people.

00:03:39.985 --> 00:03:41.320
-What was
the timeframe for that?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.524
-I would say sometime
around the 1st of November,

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.125
maybe a little before that.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.927
-I'll give Trump credit
for one thing --

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.363
he doesn't overwhelm you
with the details.

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.563
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:54.333
"We're gonna maybe
do a tax cut pretty soon.

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.903
Maybe Novemberuary...

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.504
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.573
...ish."

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.441
So Trump says Republicans
are gonna introduce

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:05.044
a major middle-class tax cut
prior to November,

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.745
which sounds great,
except for the fact

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:08.313
that Congress is out of session

00:04:08.313 --> 00:04:11.050
until after the November 6th
midterm elections.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.584
So there
are two possibilities here.

00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:13.686
Either Trump is lying,

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.654
or he doesn't know
how Congress works.

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.557
And, honestly,
it's probably both.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.824
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:19.992
If you're ever --

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:23.629
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:25.264
If you're ever asking yourself,

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:26.999
"Is Trump lying
or is he stupid?"

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:29.368
The answer is most likely,
"C," all of the above.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:30.836
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:33.172
And yet Trump keeps repeating
this obvious fabrication,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.574
hoping voters will hear it
and think Republicans

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.210
are actually going
to cut their taxes.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.778
In fact, here's an exchange
Trump had with reporters

00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:41.781
this week where they tried
to explain to him

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.749
that what he was saying
made no sense.

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:45.351
I'm gonna read
the transcript for you.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.552
Here it is.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.821
"You said that you wanted
tax cuts by November 1st.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.657
Congress isn't even in session.
How is that possible?"

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:53.259
"No, we're going
to be passing --

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:55.995
No, no, we're putting in
a resolution sometime

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:58.664
in the next week
or week and a half, two weeks."

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:00.232
"A resolution where?"

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:01.634
"We're going to put in.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.804
We're giving a middle-income
tax reduction of about 10%."

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.072
"Are you signing
an executive order for that?"

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:09.675
"No, no, no,
I'm going through Congress."

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:12.277
"But Congress isn't in session,
though.

00:05:12.277 --> 00:05:13.879
We won't have time
to do the vote."

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:15.414
"We'll do the vote later."

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.383
"Congress is out."

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:20.320
"We'll do the vote
after the election."

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.356
It's like
an Abbott and Costello routine

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:27.292
where Trump is Abbott
and Costello,

00:05:27.292 --> 00:05:29.829
and the theater has a gas leak.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:34.933
[ Applause ]

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:37.670
That transcript is like
listening to your grandpa

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.972
talk to the cable guy.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.440
"I'm trying
to change the channel."

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.741
"Sir, your TV's not on."

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:43.776
"Yes, it is."

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.144
"What channel are you watching?"

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.445
"The snowy channel."

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:47.613
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.048
Trump then repeated the same lie

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.583
at a rally in Texas
later that day,

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.751
and as he was talking about it,
he tried to ask

00:05:52.751 --> 00:05:55.320
the Congressman in charge
of tax policy, Kevin Brady,

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:58.157
who was in the crowd if what
he was saying was accurate.

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.992
-We're gonna putting in

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:04.864
a 10% tax cut
for middle-income families.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.933
It's going to be
put in next year.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:10.769
You talk about help with taxes,

00:06:10.769 --> 00:06:14.206
and so, Kevin,
we're putting in next week

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:17.943
the 10% reduction
in middle-income taxes, right?

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.078
Next week.

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.746
-"We're putting in
next week, right?

00:06:20.746 --> 00:06:22.047
No?
Why?

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:25.184
Oh! Because Congress
is out of session.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:27.520
But why?
Oh, they're campaigning!

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.388
For what?
Oh! Congress."

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:32.825
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:33.993
"What's that?"

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.294
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:36.462
But Trump --

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.629
[ Applause ]

00:06:37.629 --> 00:06:40.633
Trump isn't just lying...

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.501
Trump isn't just lying
about stuff he hasn't done.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.269
He's also lying about stuff
he has done,

00:06:44.269 --> 00:06:45.904
like his attempts
to repeal Obamacare,

00:06:45.904 --> 00:06:47.974
which protects people
with pre-existing conditions.

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:49.942
Remember, this has been
the defining fight

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.443
of the last decade of politics.

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:52.979
Republicans have spent 10 years

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:54.814
promising and then trying
to repeal Obamacare.

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:57.616
And yet, and perhaps the most
brazen lie of his presidency,

00:06:57.616 --> 00:07:00.186
Trump tweeted yesterday
and repeated again today

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:01.887
the false claim that Republicans

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.956
will protect
pre-existing conditions.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:07.426
-Quote, "Republicans
will totally protect people

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:09.328
with pre-existing conditions.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:11.230
Democrats will not.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.597
Vote Republican."

00:07:12.597 --> 00:07:15.434
-We will always
protect Americans

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:19.205
with pre-existing conditions.
Always.

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:21.941
-Dude, you just spent two years
trying to repeal the damn thing.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.141
We saw you.

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:25.711
You held a party
in the Rose Garden to celebrate.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.046
Do you remember?

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:29.215
It was you
and the cast of "Cocoon."

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:30.816
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:33.352
I mean, look at how many
old, white dudes are there.

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:34.887
[ Applause ]

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:37.022
All they need
is an acoustic guitar

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:38.591
and that press conference
could've doubled

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:40.026
as a Viagra commercial.

00:07:40.026 --> 00:07:42.528
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:46.632
And not only did the GOP try
repeatedly to repeal Obamacare,

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.701
the administration
is currently backing a lawsuit

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.769
that seeks to overturn Obamacare
and its protections

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:52.537
for people
with pre-existing conditions.

00:07:52.537 --> 00:07:55.074
And yet, in spite of this,
Trump and GOP candidates

00:07:55.074 --> 00:07:56.842
across the country have been
lying through their teeth,

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:59.545
claiming that they will maintain
those protections.

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.614
-We can protect
pre-existing conditions,

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.048
and you need to understand,

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:06.051
everyone agrees we're gonna
protect pre-existing conditions.

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:08.487
-We can protect people
with pre-existing conditions

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:12.024
in the state without protecting
the failure that is Obamacare.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:13.993
-I am passionate
about protecting people

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:16.795
with pre-existing conditions
and forcing insurance companies

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:18.531
to provide them
health insurance.

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:20.533
-I support
forcing insurance companies

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:22.835
to cover all
pre-existing conditions.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:25.337
-We support
taking care of people

00:08:25.337 --> 00:08:27.272
with pre-existing conditions.

00:08:27.272 --> 00:08:29.374
I've said it before,
I'll say it again --

00:08:29.374 --> 00:08:32.211
I'll fall in front of a truck
before I let people

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:35.380
go without coverage
for pre-existing conditions.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:38.017
-Oh, well, lucky for you,
falling in front of a truck

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:39.618
is covered under Obamacare.

00:08:39.618 --> 00:08:41.554
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:44.323
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:47.293
So, in the closing days
of the campaign,

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:49.328
Trump and the GOP
are lying brazenly

00:08:49.328 --> 00:08:51.563
about healthcare
and a made-up tax cut.

00:08:51.563 --> 00:08:53.799
And if all that fails,
Trump's fallback plan

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:55.167
is to scare the crap
out of people

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.469
by lying about immigration.

00:08:56.469 --> 00:08:59.004
In fact, we're seeing that
all over this country.

00:08:59.004 --> 00:09:01.039
Republicans are fear-mongering
about immigration,

00:09:01.039 --> 00:09:02.974
appealing to racial paranoia,
and, in some cases,

00:09:02.974 --> 00:09:04.877
running explicitly
racist campaigns

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:06.312
against their
Democratic opponents,

00:09:06.312 --> 00:09:09.514
which is why it was so cathartic
to watch this amazing exchange

00:09:09.514 --> 00:09:11.851
yesterday from Florida's
gubernatorial debate

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:15.387
between Democrat Andrew Gillum
and Republican Ron DeSantis.

00:09:15.387 --> 00:09:17.657
-Mr. DeSantis has spoken.

00:09:17.657 --> 00:09:19.158
Hey, first of all,
he's got Neo-Nazis

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:21.060
helping him out in this state.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.328
He has spoken
at racist conferences.

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:25.931
He's accepted a contribution
and would not return it

00:09:25.931 --> 00:09:27.232
from someone
who referred to

00:09:27.232 --> 00:09:28.800
the former President
of the United States

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.604
as a Muslim n-----.

00:09:32.604 --> 00:09:34.907
When asked to return that money,
he said no.

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:37.143
He's using that money
to now fund negative ads.

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:39.377
Now, I'm not calling
Mr. DeSantis a racist.

00:09:39.377 --> 00:09:41.947
I'm simply saying the racists
believe he's a racist.

00:09:41.947 --> 00:09:43.816
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:47.420
-If I may appropriate some
black culture for just a moment.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.553
Oh, snap.

00:09:48.553 --> 00:09:52.324
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:52.324 --> 00:09:53.793
I really...

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:55.260
[ Applause ]

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.496
I really hope Republicans
are right about healthcare,

00:09:57.496 --> 00:09:59.164
because after a hit like that,

00:09:59.164 --> 00:10:01.200
that dude's gonna have
a pre-existing condition.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.534
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:05.570
That debate should have gone
by "Mortal Kombat" rules.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:08.274
-I'm simply saying the racists
believe he's a racist.

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:09.608
-Finish him!

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:10.743
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:12.477
-Seriously.

00:10:12.477 --> 00:10:14.146
Look at that guy's face.

00:10:14.146 --> 00:10:15.314
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:15.314 --> 00:10:17.282
Anytime someone makes that face,

00:10:17.282 --> 00:10:19.251
it should be accompanied
by this sound.

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:22.087
[ Pac-Man dying sound ]

00:10:22.087 --> 00:10:24.156
Think about what it says
that, after two years in power,

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:26.058
all Republicans can do
is lie about healthcare,

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:27.659
make up a fictional tax cut,

00:10:27.659 --> 00:10:30.229
and try to terrify people about
a group of vulnerable migrants

00:10:30.229 --> 00:10:31.964
slowly walking
toward the border.

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:34.567
They've had two years to govern
and nothing to show for it.

00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:36.635
I'd say a lot worse
than that but...

00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:38.103
-I'm trying to be nice.

00:10:38.103 --> 00:10:39.471
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:10:39.471 --> 00:10:43.442
[ Cheers and applause ]

